{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.b359ff806f","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-329","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lake Sable is in southern Brazil. It was first surveyed in 1977.</li><li>Its surface area is 384 square kilometers.</li><li>Lake Eastwick is in northern Chile. It was first surveyed in 1925.</li><li>Its surface area is 205 square kilometers.</li><li>Both are reservoirs created by dams.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two lakes.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The surface area of Lake Sable (384 square kilometers) is greater than that of Lake Eastwick (205 square kilometers).","Lake Sable is in southern Brazil, and Lake Eastwick is in northern Chile.","Lake Sable was first surveyed in 1977, while Lake Eastwick was first surveyed in 1925.","Lake Sable, which is in southern Brazil, is one of several reservoirs created by dams."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.7c7b839938","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-343","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Glenrock Tower is in western Scotland. It was completed in 1985.</li><li>Its height is 453 meters.</li><li>The Yarrow Tower is in eastern Australia. It was completed in 1923.</li><li>Its height is 213 meters.</li><li>Both are towers built mainly of steel.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two towers.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Glenrock Tower, which is in western Scotland, is one of several towers built mainly of steel.","The Glenrock Tower was completed in 1985, while the Yarrow Tower was completed in 1923.","The height of the Glenrock Tower (453 meters) is greater than that of the Yarrow Tower (213 meters).","The Glenrock Tower is in western Scotland, and the Yarrow Tower is in eastern Australia."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.898e685814","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-367","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Wexford Observatory is in southern New Zealand. It began operating in 1914.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 11 meters.</li><li>The Orla Observatory is in eastern Poland. It began operating in 1942.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 9 meters.</li><li>Both are observatories located on remote mountaintops.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two observatorys.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Wexford Observatory, which is in southern New Zealand, is one of several observatories located on remote mountaintops.","The Wexford Observatory began operating in 1914, while the Orla Observatory began operating in 1942.","The main telescope's mirror diameter of the Wexford Observatory (11 meters) is greater than that of the Orla Observatory (9 meters).","The Wexford Observatory is in southern New Zealand, and the Orla Observatory is in eastern Poland."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.4a131b6003","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-372","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Fenwick Tower is in eastern Australia. It was completed in 1983.</li><li>Its height is 176 meters.</li><li>The Cresthill Tower is in central Spain. It was completed in 1933.</li><li>Its height is 148 meters.</li><li>Both are observation towers open to the public.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two towers.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Fenwick Tower, which is in eastern Australia, is one of several observation towers open to the public.","The height of the Fenwick Tower (176 meters) is greater than that of the Cresthill Tower (148 meters).","The Fenwick Tower is in eastern Australia, and the Cresthill Tower is in central Spain.","The Fenwick Tower was completed in 1983, while the Cresthill Tower was completed in 1933."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.e06df70b65","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-374","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Merrow Tower is in western Kenya. It was completed in 1910.</li><li>Its height is 471 meters.</li><li>The Quarry Tower is in eastern Australia. It was completed in 1900.</li><li>Its height is 116 meters.</li><li>Both are observation towers open to the public.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two towers.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Merrow Tower was completed in 1910, while the Quarry Tower was completed in 1900.","The Merrow Tower, which is in western Kenya, is one of several observation towers open to the public.","The height of the Merrow Tower (471 meters) is greater than that of the Quarry Tower (116 meters).","The Merrow Tower is in western Kenya, and the Quarry Tower is in eastern Australia."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.34442f760a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-376","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Alder Museum is in eastern Poland. It opened in 1944.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 493,418 visitors.</li><li>The Merrow Museum is in northern Chile. It opened in 2016.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 442,176 visitors.</li><li>Both are art museums with free admission.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two museums.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The annual attendance of the Alder Museum (493,418 visitors) is greater than that of the Merrow Museum (442,176 visitors).","The Alder Museum opened in 1944, while the Merrow Museum opened in 2016.","The Alder Museum, which is in eastern Poland, is one of several art museums with free admission.","The Alder Museum is in eastern Poland, and the Merrow Museum is in northern Chile."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.c3e3beb4be","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-390","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Valewood Tunnel is in southern Norway. It opened in 1999.</li><li>Its length is 11 kilometers.</li><li>The Eastwick Tunnel is in southern New Zealand. It opened in 2011.</li><li>Its length is 5 kilometers.</li><li>Both are railway tunnels.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two tunnels.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The length of the Valewood Tunnel (11 kilometers) is greater than that of the Eastwick Tunnel (5 kilometers).","The Valewood Tunnel is in southern Norway, and the Eastwick Tunnel is in southern New Zealand.","The Valewood Tunnel opened in 1999, while the Eastwick Tunnel opened in 2011.","The Valewood Tunnel, which is in southern Norway, is one of several railway tunnels."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.c591bc8baa","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-394","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lake Halden is in eastern Poland. It was first surveyed in 1911.</li><li>Its surface area is 854 square kilometers.</li><li>Lake Dunmore is in central Spain. It was first surveyed in 1978.</li><li>Its surface area is 658 square kilometers.</li><li>Both are reservoirs created by dams.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two lakes.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Lake Halden was first surveyed in 1911, while Lake Dunmore was first surveyed in 1978.","Lake Halden is in eastern Poland, and Lake Dunmore is in central Spain.","Lake Halden, which is in eastern Poland, is one of several reservoirs created by dams.","The surface area of Lake Halden (854 square kilometers) is greater than that of Lake Dunmore (658 square kilometers)."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.2f1986cae9","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-7","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Mensah is an ecologist.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether city lights change when songbirds begin singing in the morning.</li><li>Mensah compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands.</li><li>Mensah found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.</li><li>Mensah concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mensah found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.","Because robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier, Mensah concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.","Mensah concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.","To investigate the question, Mensah compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.7fac35924b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-18","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Diego Haddad is an agricultural scientist.</li><li>Haddad wanted to find out whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.</li><li>Haddad grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.</li><li>Haddad found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.</li><li>Haddad concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Haddad found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.","Haddad concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.","Because fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer, Haddad concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.","To investigate the question, Haddad grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.b922761d9d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-34","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Takeda is an entomologist.</li><li>Takeda wanted to find out whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.</li><li>Takeda set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.</li><li>Takeda found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.</li><li>Takeda concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Takeda set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.","Takeda found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.","Because bees visited the blue feeders most often, Takeda concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.","Takeda concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.58090f38d0","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-37","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Dmitri Castellano is a sociologist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another.</li><li>Castellano surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.</li><li>Castellano found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.</li><li>Castellano concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened, Castellano concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.","Castellano found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.","To investigate the question, Castellano surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.","Castellano concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.3d659d5636","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-40","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Imani Delacroix is a sociologist.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether community gardens increase how often neighbors talk to one another.</li><li>Delacroix surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.</li><li>Delacroix found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Delacroix concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.","Because residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened, Delacroix concluded that community gardens may strengthen neighborhood ties.","To investigate the question, Delacroix surveyed residents before and one year after gardens opened in their neighborhoods.","Delacroix found that residents reported speaking with neighbors more often after the gardens opened."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.81946f11a0","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-47","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Dmitri Mensah is a geologist.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether a hillside's plant cover affects how much soil washes away in heavy rain.</li><li>Mensah measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses.</li><li>Mensah found that bare slopes lost several times more soil.</li><li>Mensah concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mensah concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.","To investigate the question, Mensah measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses.","Because bare slopes lost several times more soil, Mensah concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.","Mensah found that bare slopes lost several times more soil."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.49a8cd8e89","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-57","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Leila Kowalski is a zoologist.</li><li>Kowalski wanted to find out whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active.</li><li>Kowalski gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.</li><li>Kowalski found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.</li><li>Kowalski concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Kowalski gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.","Because elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day, Kowalski concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.","Kowalski concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.","Kowalski found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.045b5c5f75","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-96","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Hana Brennan is an education researcher.</li><li>Brennan wanted to find out whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.</li><li>Brennan had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.</li><li>Brennan found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.</li><li>Brennan concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Brennan had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.","Brennan found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.","Because children in the read-aloud group learned more new words, Brennan concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.","Brennan concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.2199d8c6a7","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-97","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Sofia Quintero is an education researcher.</li><li>Quintero wanted to find out whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.</li><li>Quintero had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.</li><li>Quintero found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.</li><li>Quintero concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Quintero had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.","Quintero concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.","Quintero found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.","Because children in the read-aloud group learned more new words, Quintero concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.36c476df0c","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-134","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Duarte is an archaeologist.</li><li>Duarte wanted to find out whether a coastal settlement traded with inland villages.</li><li>Duarte analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement.</li><li>Duarte found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland.</li><li>Duarte concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Duarte found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland.","Duarte concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.","Because many pots were made from clay found only far inland, Duarte concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.","To investigate the question, Duarte analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.d85b13280e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-139","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Asante is a neuroscientist.</li><li>Asante wanted to find out whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.</li><li>Asante scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.</li><li>Asante found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.</li><li>Asante concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Asante scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.","Asante found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.","Because regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger, Asante concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.","Asante concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.fb8fdef2eb","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-146","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Hana Iyer is a marine ecologist.</li><li>Iyer wanted to find out whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests.</li><li>Iyer fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.</li><li>Iyer found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.</li><li>Iyer concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Iyer fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.","Iyer found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.","Iyer concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.","Because kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser, Iyer concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.4a483a2ac7","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-158","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Yara Nakamura is a behavioral economist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance.</li><li>Nakamura moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.</li><li>Nakamura found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Nakamura concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.","Because fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays, Nakamura concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.","Nakamura found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.","To investigate the question, Nakamura moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.e9ce98d8a1","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-161","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jonas Solberg is a behavioral economist.</li><li>Solberg wanted to find out whether shoppers buy more fruit when it is placed near the store entrance.</li><li>Solberg moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others.</li><li>Solberg found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.</li><li>Solberg concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Solberg concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.","Solberg found that fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays.","Because fruit sales rose in the stores with entrance displays, Solberg concluded that product placement may influence shoppers' choices.","To investigate the question, Solberg moved the fruit display to the entrance in some stores but not others."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.130d5ff57e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-167","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Castellano is a veterinary scientist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether dogs recognize their owners' voices.</li><li>Castellano played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs.</li><li>Castellano found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often.</li><li>Castellano concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Castellano found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often.","To investigate the question, Castellano played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs.","Because dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often, Castellano concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.","Castellano concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.ea74e8f640","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-168","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Viktor Kowalski is a forest ecologist.</li><li>Kowalski wanted to find out whether fungi help trees share nutrients.</li><li>Kowalski added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.</li><li>Kowalski found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.</li><li>Kowalski concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Kowalski found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.","Kowalski concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.","Because the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks, Kowalski concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.","To investigate the question, Kowalski added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.cb6e64c74d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-173","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Maren Iyer is a forest ecologist.</li><li>Iyer wanted to find out whether fungi help trees share nutrients.</li><li>Iyer added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.</li><li>Iyer found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.</li><li>Iyer concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Iyer concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.","To investigate the question, Iyer added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.","Iyer found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.","Because the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks, Iyer concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.6904282e3a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-178","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Mensah is a music researcher.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether learning an instrument improves children's listening skills.</li><li>Mensah tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.</li><li>Mensah found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.</li><li>Mensah concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mensah concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.","Mensah found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.","To investigate the question, Mensah tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.","Because children who took lessons improved more than those who did not, Mensah concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."}
